因为如果大家关心的是同样的东西，那他们就会部署相同的拥塞控制算法。
Because if everyone cares about the same thing, then they would be deploying the same congestion control algorithms.

35
00:04:22,574 --> 00:04:32,356
而人们之所以在今天部署不同的拥塞控制算法，是因为现在的
拥塞控制算法也体现了应用程序对吞吐量和延迟权衡的需求。
And the reason people are deploying different congestion control algorithms today is because today congestion control algorithms also
capture an application's desired throughput delay trade-offs.

36
00:04:32,846 --> 00:04:40,772
根据你的应用程序更看重吞吐量还是延迟，他们可能会部署不同的拥塞控制算法。
Depending on what your application cares about, whether it's more throughput or more delay,
they might deploy different congestion control algorithms.

37
00:04:41,102 --> 00:04:47,300
这些确实是我们测量研究中看到的趋势，我们在研究谁部署了什么样的拥塞控制算法。
And these are indeed trends that we saw in our measurement study where
we were measuring who was deploying what congestion control algorithms.

38
00:04:48,206 --> 00:04:54,116
只要看看这些拥塞控制算法是如何运行的，我们就能理解其中的原因。
And we can understand why this is the case when we simply look at how some of these congestion control algorithms operate.

39
00:04:54,990 --> 00:04:58,948
例如，这里我有两个在 Linux 内核中的拥塞控制算法。
So for example, over here, I have two congestion control algorithms in the Linux kernel.

40
00:04:59,280 --> 00:05:01,924
你们可能听说过它们，就是 Cubic 和 Vegas。
You've probably heard about them, Cubic and Vegas.

41
00:05:02,734 --> 00:05:08,932
在这里，我在相同的网络中运行它们，网络拥有 100 Mbps 的链路和 10 BDP 的缓冲区。
Over here, I ran them through identical networks that had 100 Mbps links in a 10 BDP buffer.

42
00:05:09,326 --> 00:05:14,404
我们看到在相同的环境下，它们做出了非常不同的吞吐量与延迟权衡。
And we see that in identical circumstances, they make very different throughput delay trade-offs.

43
00:05:14,990 --> 00:05:31,120
我们可以看到 Vegas 恰好是延迟优化，它选择最小化延迟；而 Cubic 试图进行吞吐量优化，
它希望把数据包放入缓冲区以最大化吞吐量。
So we can see Vegas, which happens to be delay optimizing, chooses to make to minimize delay, whereas Cubic,
which tries to be throughput optimizing, wants to put packets in the buffer in order to maximize throughput.

44
00:05:31,406 --> 00:05:36,900
正是这些不同的目标导致了它们之间的不公平。
And it's these different goals that sort of motivate, that sort of create the unfairness between them.

45
00:05:37,230 --> 00:05:50,148
因为如果我重复这个实验，这次我强制 Cubic 和 Vegas 使用相同的瓶颈链路，
Cubic 会抢走大部分带宽，而 Vegas 流会因为试图最小化延迟而陷入饥饿。
Because if I repeat this experiment and this time I force Cubic and Vegas to use the same bottleneck link,
Cubic steals most of the bandwidth while Vegas flow starves because it tries to minimize the delay.

46
00:05:50,734 --> 00:06:02,960
